{% set runners = run.runners | join(", ") %}
## {{ run.heading }}

{% if run.runners %}
The board runs the hub, and beside it each {{ runners }} runner the scenario places on it, compiled into the
firmware from its module's component. The build refuses a runner that imports what the board
does not host, or runners needing more memory than it holds.
The board serves this scenario's modules from its {{ run.flash_size }} of flash.
{% else %}
The board runs the hub alone and serves this scenario's modules from its {{ run.flash_size }} of flash.
{% endif %}
{% include "readme/load-board.md.j2" %}

To check what the board will serve without one, serve the same modules from this host and fetch
each, as a page would:

```bash
{{ run.host_test }}
```

The board takes an address over DHCP and serves the page at port 8080 of it. npm packages the
modules use that are too big for its flash, such as onnxruntime-web, are not built in: the board
redirects a request for one to the same path under `{{ run.elsewhere }}`, which the browser has to be
able to reach.
